From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: say when a native task or mesh draw asks for
 instances

Core patch on mig020-core (T42). A log line, once per run, on a path T42 never reaches: with
EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH set no mesh draw gets this far.

The native mesh draw calls DrawMeshTasksEXT(groups, 1, 1) and drops the draw's instance count without
a word. The core's own compute path already logs this. Same line here, so a plant test can tell a
draw that lost its instances from one that worked.

Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -1017,6 +1017,15 @@
                 }
                 return;
             }
+            // Instances are not run here either: say so, or a draw that lost them looks like any
+            // other in a plant test.
+            if (num_instances > 1) {
+                static bool logged{};
+                if (!std::exchange(logged, true)) {
+                    LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "Task/mesh draw with {} instances: one run",
+                                num_instances);
+                }
+            }
             scheduler.Record([this, groups](vk::CommandBuffer cmdbuf) {
                 if (scheduler.GraphicsPipelineMissing()) {
                     return;
